<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold prices seen mixed on subdued demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold prices seen mixed on subdued demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold prices are likely to remain mixed this week amid subdued demand, Karachi dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Dealer Farooq Qureshi said inflation had eroded savings and buying power, depressing demand.</p>
<p>He said silver prices would also remain stable on low demand for silver jewellery.</p>
<p>							 Saturday   April 26</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grams   4,565	4,612</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   6,687	6,687</p>
<p>($1 = 40.34 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
